-- 13  Narrowly scoped SECURITY DEFINER authentication functions
--
-- Why definer functions exist at all: before a tenant context can be
-- established the server must (a) verify credentials, (b) list the caller's
-- tenant memberships and (c) validate the session / refresh token.  Those rows
-- are tenant-isolated by RLS, so a context-free lookup is impossible for the
-- service roles by design.  Each function below:
--   * is owned by the NOLOGIN role rag_auth_fn (no BYPASSRLS, no superuser);
--     rag_auth_fn's policies are the only ones that allow a cross-tenant read,
--     and only on identity / session tables (never content);
--   * pins search_path to pg_catalog, pg_temp (no search-path hijacking);
--   * returns the minimum columns needed;
--   * is EXECUTE-able only by rag_app (REVOKE FROM PUBLIC).
-- See docs/security/DATABASE_SECURITY.md.
